{"total_count":24,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68299","id":5102006297,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde878mzVb","number":68299,"title":"[Blazor] Generate component metadata for Native AOT","user":{"login":"javiercn","id":6995051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6995051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn","html_url":"https://github.com/javiercn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5058451585,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABLYHYgQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/pending-ci-rerun","name":"pending-ci-rerun","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"When assigned to a PR indicates that the CI checks should be rerun","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-09T10:15:38Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T00:47:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/68299","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68299","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68299.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68299.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Overview\n\nThis is layer 4 of 6 for [#68332](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68332), stacked on #68297. It gives component activation, member access, routing/discovery, and Server root operations one shared `ComponentTypeInfo` model, then teaches the application metadata generator to produce that model at compile time. The governing constraint is **generated first, reflection last**: registered metadata avoids reflection, while applications without metadata continue to work unchanged; framework-owned descriptor providers and strict reflection disablement remain in later stack layers.\n\n## Design\n\nThe new experimental contract describes a component as executable metadata rather than as reflected members:\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Components/src/Infrastructure/ComponentDescriptor.cs\n// One complete application-component description: construction, bindable members, injection,\n// and the attribute-shaped metadata already consumed by routing/rendering.\n[Experimental(\"ASPNETCORE9004\", UrlFormat = \"https://aka.ms/aspnet/analyzer/{0}\")]\npublic sealed class ComponentDescriptor\n{\n    [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.All)]\n    public required Type Type { get; init; }\n    public Func<IServiceProvider, IComponent>? CreateInstance { get; init; }\n    public IReadOnlyList<ComponentParameterDescriptor> Parameters { get; init; } = [];\n    public IReadOnlyList<ComponentInjectableDescriptor> Injectables { get; init; } = [];\n    public IReadOnlyList<object> Metadata { get; init; } = [];\n}\n```\n\n`ComponentParameterDescriptor` carries the declared type, role attribute, generated getter/setter delegates, and an optional closed persistent-state serializer factory. `ComponentInjectableDescriptor` is separate because injection has different semantics: service type, keyed `[Inject]` metadata, and a setter, but no getter or unmatched-value behavior. The open metadata bag carries route, layout, render-mode, endpoint, and future attributes without expanding the public API for each feature.\n\nThe existing application metadata context gains one capability and keeps the lower-layer JSON, JS-invokable, and bindable contracts:\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Web/src/Metadata/RazorComponentsMetadataContext.cs\npublic abstract class RazorComponentsMetadataContext\n{\n    public abstract IReadOnlyList<ComponentDescriptor> Components { get; }\n    public abstract IReadOnlyList<BindableTypeDescriptor> BindableTypes { get; }\n    public abstract IReadOnlyList<JSInvokableMethodDescriptor> JSInvokableMethods { get; }\n    public abstract IJsonTypeInfoResolver? JsonTypeInfoResolver { get; }\n}\n```\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Web/src/Metadata/ComponentMetadataServiceCollectionExtensions.cs\npublic static IServiceCollection AddComponentMetadata<TContext>(this IServiceCollection services)\n    where TContext : RazorComponentsMetadataContext, new()\n{\n    var context = new TContext();\n    services.Configure<ComponentDescriptorOptions>(options =>\n    {\n        foreach (var component in context.Components)\n        {\n            options.Components.Add(component);\n        }\n    });\n\n    services.AddSingleton<RazorComponentsMetadataContext>(context);\n    services.TryAddSingleton<IComponentMetadataResolver>(\n        static services => services.GetRequiredService<ComponentMetadataResolver>());\n    services.TryAddSingleton<IComponentTypeInfoResolver>(ComponentTypeInfoResolverFactory.Create);\n    return services;\n}\n```\n\nTwo decisions preserve compatibility:\n\n- A component is generated **completely or not at all**. A partial descriptor could silently omit a parameter or injected property because runtime consumers trust the descriptor's member lists. Unsupported/inaccessible application components receive a diagnostic and remain on reflection.\n- The runtime owns the component-reflection feature switch, but its default stays `true`. This layer defines generated-only resolver/failure semantics; the final strict layer is responsible for setting the switch to `false`.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Components/src/ComponentTypeInfoResolverFactory.cs\ninternal static IComponentTypeInfoResolver Create(IServiceProvider services)\n{\n    var resolvers = new List<IComponentTypeInfoResolver>();\n    if (services.GetService<IComponentMetadataResolver>() is { } metadataResolver)\n    {\n        resolvers.Add(new SourceGeneratedComponentTypeInfoResolver(metadataResolver));\n    }\n\n    if (ComponentMetadataFeature.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault)\n    {\n        resolvers.Add(new ReflectionComponentTypeInfoResolver());\n    }\n\n    return new CompositeComponentTypeInfoResolver(resolvers);\n}\n```\n\nFramework assemblies are intentionally skipped by the application collector. The next stack layer supplies owner-authored framework descriptors and factories; this PR only establishes the resolver/merge contract they consume.\n\n## Implementation\n\nA renderer creates one resolver chain and gives it to activation, property injection, parameter binding, cascading state, persistence, discovery, and root operations. The source-generated resolver is first; the composite caches type/name/assembly lookups, can fill a missing generated construction factory from a later resolver, and invalidates caches for hot reload. If both generated and reflection resolvers exist, hot reload disables stale generated descriptors and continues through reflection.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Components/src/RenderTree/Renderer.cs\nvar registeredTypeInfoResolver = serviceProvider.GetService<IComponentTypeInfoResolver>();\nComponentTypeInfoResolver = registeredTypeInfoResolver\n    ?? ComponentTypeInfoResolverFactory.Create(serviceProvider);\n\ncomponentActivator ??= serviceProvider.GetService<IComponentActivator>()\n    ?? new DefaultComponentActivator(serviceProvider, ComponentTypeInfoResolver);\nvar propertyActivator = serviceProvider.GetService<IComponentPropertyActivator>()\n    ?? new DefaultComponentPropertyActivator(ComponentTypeInfoResolver);\n_componentFactory = new ComponentFactory(componentActivator, propertyActivator, this);\n```\n\nThe generator walks referenced application types with private metadata imported because Razor-generated `@inject` properties and render-mode attributes are not visible under Roslyn's default import mode. It preserves most-derived member semantics, reconstructs component attributes, and rejects the whole component if any required member cannot be reached.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Endpoints/gen/RazorComponentsMetadataGenerator.Components.cs\n// A partial descriptor is unsafe: consumers would trust incomplete parameter/injection lists.\nif (!TryDescribeComponent(type, types, generatedIn, diagnostics, out var model, out var reason))\n{\n    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(reason))\n    {\n        diagnostics.Add(new DiagnosticInfo(\n            DiagnosticDescriptors.ComponentNotFullyDescribed.Id,\n            type.FullName(),\n            reason));\n    }\n\n    continue;\n}\n```\n\nGenerated parameter descriptors cover ordinary, cascading/query/session/TempData, and persistent parameters. Their deltas are only the reconstructed attribute and optional serializer/accessor bridge:\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Endpoints/gen/Emitters/RazorComponentsMetadataGenerator.Emitter.cs\nwriter.WriteLine($\"Name = {SymbolHelpers.ToStringLiteral(parameter.Name)},\");\nwriter.WriteLine($\"ParameterType = typeof({parameter.PropertyTypeFullyQualifiedName}),\");\nwriter.WriteLine($\"Attribute = {parameter.AttributeExpression},\");\nwriter.WriteLine($\"SetValue = static (__target, __value) => {write},\");\nwriter.WriteLine($\"GetValue = static __target => {read},\");\n\nif (parameter.IsPersistentState)\n{\n    // T is known at compile time, avoiding MakeGenericType at runtime.\n    writer.WriteLine(\n        $\"GetStateSerializer = static __services => __services.GetService(\" +\n        $\"typeof({StateSerializerType}<{parameter.PropertyTypeFullyQualifiedName}>)),\");\n}\n```\n\nRuntime entry points retain renderer-scoped type info instead of rediscovering members. `ComponentBase` binds through the renderer; `ComponentFactory` uses descriptor render modes, activation, and injection; Session and TempData share descriptor-first value access instead of maintaining independent reflection caches.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Components/src/ComponentBase.cs\npublic virtual Task SetParametersAsync(ParameterView parameters)\n{\n    parameters.SetParameterProperties(this, _renderHandle);\n    if (!_initialized)\n    {\n        _initialized = true;\n        return RunInitAndSetParametersAsync();\n    }\n\n    return CallOnParametersSetAsync();\n}\n```\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Endpoints/src/ComponentParameterValueGetter.cs\ninternal static Func<object?> Create(object component, ComponentTypeInfo typeInfo, string propertyName)\n{\n    var descriptor = FindParameter(typeInfo, propertyName);\n    if (descriptor is null && ComponentMetadataFeature.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault)\n    {\n        descriptor = FindParameter(\n            ComponentTypeInfoResolverFactory.Default.GetRequiredTypeInfo(component.GetType()),\n            propertyName);\n    }\n\n    if (descriptor is null)\n    {\n        throw new InvalidOperationException(\n            $\"A property '{propertyName}' on component type '{component.GetType().FullName}' wasn't found.\");\n    }\n\n    return () => descriptor.GetValue(component);\n}\n```\n\nDiscovery is the assembly-enumeration equivalence class. Routing and endpoint discovery enumerate `ComponentTypeInfo`, route-cache identity includes the resolver, and endpoint metadata is the descriptor metadata minus `RouteAttribute`. Layout and render-mode consumers read the same metadata bag, so the old assembly/component/page builder graph is removed.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Endpoints/src/Discovery/ComponentApplicationBuilder.cs\npublic ComponentApplicationBuilder AddAssembly(Assembly assembly)\n{\n    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(assembly);\n    AddLibrary(assembly.FullName!, _typeInfoResolver.GetRequiredTypeInfos(assembly));\n    return this;\n}\n```\n\nServer roots are the lifetime equivalence class. Initial marker deserialization resolves and stores `ComponentTypeInfo`; dynamic add/update operations pass that object into the renderer; resumed circuits retain `(typeInfo, parameters)` rather than discarding metadata and resolving by `Type` again.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Shared/src/WebRootComponentManager.cs\npublic Task AddRootComponentAsync(\n    int ssrComponentId,\n    [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(Component)] Type componentType,\n    ComponentMarkerKey? key,\n    WebRootComponentParameters parameters)\n    => AddRootComponentAsync(\n        ssrComponentId,\n        renderer.ComponentTypeInfoResolver.GetRequiredTypeInfo(componentType),\n        key,\n        parameters);\n```\n\nPR4's feature application and browser scenarios now consume the Native AOT Components.Testing harness from main (#68289) and the shared MSTest/MTP infrastructure from #67083. The upstream harness owns publish/source-generation plumbing; this PR contributes only its application, `ServerFactory` fixture/routing integration, and component-metadata scenarios. The separate `JitDefault` category proves undescribed component, JS method, and JSON payload fallbacks remain compatible.\n\n## Outcome\n\n| Equivalence class | What is covered | Validation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Runtime type-info consumers | Reflection/generated activation and injection, ordinary/cascading/query/session/TempData parameters, unmatched values, persistence, render modes, resolver ordering/caches/hot reload, activator substitution, and reflection-disabled fail-fast behavior | Focused Components: **124 passed** |\n| Discovery and endpoint value access | Type-info route/endpoint discovery, metadata propagation, descriptor-first Session/TempData getters, reflection compatibility, and missing-metadata failure | Focused Endpoints: **35 passed** |\n| Server root lifetime | Initial markers, dynamic roots, resumed roots, parameter deserialization, circuit persistence, and service registration retain `ComponentTypeInfo` | Focused Server: **123 passed** |\n| Application generation | Factories, inherited/public/private accessors, attributes, diagnostics, persistent serializer closure, typed JSON/JS serialization, and `DynamicallyAccessedMembers` bridges | Shared MSTest generator Test target: **40 passed** |\n| Feature integration | The PR4 feature project builds on the upstream Components.Testing harness and exercises generated activation plus default reflection compatibility under JIT | MSTest/MTP JIT smoke: **2 passed** |\n\nStack note: this PR depends on #68297. Framework-owned component descriptor providers are added by the next stack layer; strict reflection-disabled Native AOT proof follows after that.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68299/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70261","id":6172272997,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABMa7ttA","number":70261,"title":"Unquarantine TempData cookie persistence test","user":{"login":"BrennanConroy","id":7574801,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NzQ4MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7574801?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy","html_url":"https://github.com/BrennanConroy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrennanConroy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-02T22:34:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T19:36:19Z","closed_at":"2026-11-03T19:36:18Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70261","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70261","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70261.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70261.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #70085.\n\n`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.E2ETest.Tests.TempDataCookieTest.TempDataPersistWithoutAccessing` was quarantined after intermittent `StaleElementReferenceException` failures at `WebElement.Click()` (5 distinct builds in the issue's deterministic 30-day snapshot).\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe test runs with `PageLoadStrategy.None`. Before #70088, it submitted `set-values-not-read` and immediately searched for `redirect-button`, an ID present on both the departing `/tempdata` page and the destination `/tempdata/redirect_without_read` page. Selenium could return the departing page's element while navigation was replacing that document, making the reference stale at click time.\n\n#70088 fixed the causal race by assigning the destination button the unique ID `redirect-without-read-button` and waiting for that destination-only element with `Browser.Exists(...)`. The final TempData persistence assertion remains unchanged. This PR restores the cookie-backed test to the normal suite now that the causal fix is on `main`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exact test passed with Chrome 156.0.8078.73 and matching ChromeDriver 156.0.8078.73.\n- Repeated the exact fully qualified test 50 times: 50/50 passed.\n- The targeted test command rebuilt `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.E2ETests` and its required product/test assets successfully before execution.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## CI status\n\nAll completed non-Components-E2E checks pass, including code check, source-build, platform tests, Helix subsets, quarantined tests, and template tests. Components E2E CoreCLR also passes.\n\nBuild Analysis attributes the two failed Components E2E jobs to unrelated existing flakes:\n\n- `VirtualizationTest.VariableHeight_HtmlTable_DoesNotProduceNestedTrElements` failed in Mono client/WebAssembly with an empty rendered collection; Build Analysis reports a 13.68% historical failure rate.\n- `ServerRoutingTest.NavigationLock_CanBlockExternalNavigation` failed in Mono server because navigation remained at `/subdir/`; Build Analysis reports a 31.10% historical failure rate.\n\nNeither test or subsystem is changed by this PR. A one-time GitHub check re-request was attempted for both jobs, but the Azure Pipelines integration rejected it with `403 Resource not accessible by integration`; an authorized Azure rerun is required.\n\nAfter a full repository `npm run build` and targeted E2E rebuild at this exact head, both unrelated failing tests passed locally with Chrome/ChromeDriver 156:\n\n- `VirtualizationTest.VariableHeight_HtmlTable_DoesNotProduceNestedTrElements`: passed.\n- `ServerRoutingTest.NavigationLock_CanBlockExternalNavigation`: passed.\n\n## Residual uncertainty\n\nThe original race is timing-dependent, so a finite local stress run cannot prove absence of every browser scheduling variant. The selector now cannot match the departing document, directly removing the stale-reference mechanism recorded in #70085.\n\n**🤖 Posted by Flaky (AI Agent)**\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70261/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1143301,"client_id":"Iv23ctzlsVrAf9UtZ48B","slug":"copilot-swe-agent","node_id":"A_kwHNJr_OABFyBQ","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Copilot SWE Agent","description":"","external_url":"https://github.com/features/copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","created_at":"2025-02-12T20:26:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T17:13:09Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","actions_variables":"read","administration":"read","agent_secrets":"read","agent_tasks":"write","agent_variables":"read","checks":"read","code_quality":"read","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","discussions":"write","environments":"write","gists":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","organization_agent_secrets":"read","organization_agent_variables":"read","organization_noodles":"write","packages":"read","plugin_gateway_connections":"write","pull_requests":"write","secrets":"read","secret_scanning_alerts":"read","security_events":"read","statuses":"read","vulnerability_alerts":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":[]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70088","id":6099096247,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABLgxhBw","number":70088,"title":"Fix TempData persistence test navigation race","user":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6217355196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABcpVPvA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/feature-blazor-ssr","name":"feature-blazor-ssr","color":"bfdadc","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/408","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408/labels","id":17341069,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84BCJqN","number":408,"title":"12.0-preview1","description":null,"creator":{"login":"dotnet-milestone-bot[bot]","id":286398033,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOERIWUQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9141961?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dotnet-milestone-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":6,"closed_issues":579,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-08-17T16:20:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T22:43:39Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-29T11:56:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T15:04:00Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T10:28:07Z","assignee":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70088","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70088","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70088.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70088.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-30T10:28:07Z"},"body":"# Fix TempData persistence test navigation race\r\n\r\nWait for the destination page in TempData persistence tests.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\n`TempDataPersistWithoutAccessing` submits a form and immediately clicks `redirect-button`, which exists on both the departing and destination pages. With the streaming browser's `PageLoadStrategy.None`, the test can locate the departing page's button before navigation replaces its document, causing a stale-element failure before the persistence assertion.\r\n\r\nGive the unread destination page's button a distinct ID and wait for it with `Browser.Exists(...)` in both the cookie and session-storage tests. Keep the final `Message` assertion unchanged; do not retry submissions or add sleeps. This addresses the failure investigated in #69997.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70088/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68295","id":5099066539,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde878eFaR","number":68295,"title":"[Blazor] Make component serialization metadata-first","user":{"login":"javiercn","id":6995051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTUwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6995051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn","html_url":"https://github.com/javiercn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javiercn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5058451585,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABLYHYgQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/pending-ci-rerun","name":"pending-ci-rerun","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"When assigned to a PR indicates that the CI checks should be rerun","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-08T19:19:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T00:47:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/68295","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68295","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68295.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68295.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Overview\n\nThis is stack layer **1/6** for [#68332 — Aspire Dashboard Native AOT support](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68332), bounded to the live PR diff `66e8a029..9ca33ec5` (77 files, 14 commits). It makes Blazor’s serialization boundaries metadata-first: framework contracts are source-generated, application contracts compose ahead of compatibility reflection, and converter-owned JS types remain converter-backed. The cross-cutting constraint is **host isolation**: application resolvers are snapshotted per service provider/host and never mutate process-static serializer options; later stack layers build on this JSON foundation for JS dispatch, binding, component metadata, framework providers, and the final Native AOT proof.\n\n## Design\n\nThe application-facing JSON surface is deliberately narrow and experimental: one context property and one registration method. It does not expose component, binding, or JS-invokable descriptors owned by later layers.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Web/src/Metadata/RazorComponentsMetadataContext.cs\n// Applications expose an STJ resolver without giving framework consumers direct access\n// to JsonSerializerContext instances or to unrelated component metadata.\n[Experimental(\"ASPNETCORE9004\", UrlFormat = \"https://aka.ms/aspnet/analyzer/{0}\")]\npublic abstract class RazorComponentsMetadataContext\n{\n    protected RazorComponentsMetadataContext()\n    {\n    }\n\n    public abstract IJsonTypeInfoResolver? JsonTypeInfoResolver { get; }\n}\n\n// src/Components/Web/src/Metadata/ComponentMetadataServiceCollectionExtensions.cs\n// Each registration contributes to options used to construct an immutable provider snapshot.\npublic static IServiceCollection AddComponentMetadata<TContext>(this IServiceCollection services)\n    where TContext : RazorComponentsMetadataContext, new()\n{\n    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(services);\n\n    services.AddComponentJsonMetadata();\n    var context = new TContext();\n    if (context.JsonTypeInfoResolver is { } resolver)\n    {\n        services.Configure<ComponentJsonMetadataOptions>(options => options.Resolvers.Add(resolver));\n    }\n    services.AddSingleton<RazorComponentsMetadataContext>(context);\n\n    return services;\n}\n```\n\nProtected browser storage adds typed writes and an optional typed serializer while retaining the shipped object overloads, existing constructors, and JSON fallback behavior.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Server/src/ProtectedBrowserStorage/ProtectedBrowserStorage.cs\n// Existing object overloads remain. The generic overload roots the closed TValue service lookup.\npublic ValueTask SetAsync<TValue>(string key, TValue value)\n    => SetAsync(CreatePurposeFromKey(key), key, value);\n\npublic ValueTask SetAsync<TValue>(string purpose, string key, TValue value)\n{\n    ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(purpose);\n    ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(key);\n\n    return SetProtectedJsonAsync(key, Protect(purpose, value));\n}\n\n// src/Components/Server/src/ProtectedBrowserStorage/ProtectedBrowserStorageSerializer.cs\n[Experimental(\"ASPNETCORE9004\", UrlFormat = \"https://aka.ms/aspnet/analyzer/{0}\")]\npublic abstract class ProtectedBrowserStorageSerializer<T>\n{\n    public abstract string Serialize(T value);\n    public abstract T Deserialize(string data);\n}\n```\n\nResolver ordering is intentional and consistent:\n\n| Boundary | Resolver order |\n|---|---|\n| Fixed framework DTOs | generated framework context → reflection when enabled |\n| Marker/persistence/application payloads | generated framework context → registered application resolver(s) → reflection when enabled |\n| Web/JS interop | fixed Web context → fixed JS context → converter-backed types → application resolver(s) → reflection when enabled |\n| Protected storage | application resolver(s) → reflection when enabled; custom `ProtectedBrowserStorageSerializer<T>` wins before JSON |\n\nThe rejected alternative was process-static mutation of persistence or marker resolver chains. Instead, serializer/deserializer instances, `ComponentStatePersistenceManager`, renderers, and the WebAssembly host own their options snapshots. Therefore a provider already built is immutable; only providers built after another `AddComponentMetadata<TContext>()` call observe the new contracts.\n\n## Implementation\n\n**Framework-owned contracts.** The same generated-contract pattern covers four equivalence classes; one representative is shown, with the remaining deltas listed rather than repeated:\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Server/src/CircuitJavaScriptInitializationMiddleware.cs\n// IList<string> is a closed framework payload, so the endpoint works even when STJ reflection is disabled.\npublic async Task InvokeAsync(HttpContext context)\n{\n    await context.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(\n        _initializers,\n        JavaScriptInitializersJsonContext.Default.IListString);\n}\n\n[JsonSerializable(typeof(IList<string>))]\nprivate sealed partial class JavaScriptInitializersJsonContext : JsonSerializerContext;\n```\n\n- **Static framework data:** import maps, resource collections, JavaScript initializer manifests/responses, and prerender application-state dictionaries use generated `JsonTypeInfo` overloads.\n- **Closed value families:** TempData generates its supported primitive, nullable, collection, dictionary, object-array, and `Dictionary<string, JsonElement>` shapes; generic-interface reflection remains available only when `JsonSerializer.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault`.\n- **Circuit/persistence DTOs:** circuit root-operation batches, persisted marker dictionaries, persistent-service registrations, framework persistent primitives, and antiforgery state have generated contracts.\n- **Marker/render-fragment DTOs:** Server and WebAssembly envelopes, component parameter definitions, and serialized render-tree nodes are generated; application parameter values deliberately continue into the application/reflection portion of the chain.\n\n**Protocol options remain authoritative.** Generated metadata is resolved through the protocol-owned options rather than serializing directly with a context property. This preserves camel-case field names and null omission while avoiding reflection.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Shared/Components/ServerComponentSerializationSettings.cs\n// Example wire shape remains {\"type\":\"webassembly\",...}, never {\"Type\":\"webassembly\",...}.\ninternal static JsonSerializerOptions CreateOptions(IJsonTypeInfoResolver? applicationResolver)\n{\n    var options = new JsonSerializerOptions\n    {\n        PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase,\n        PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true,\n        DefaultIgnoreCondition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull\n    };\n\n    options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(ServerComponentJsonContext.Default);\n    if (applicationResolver is not null)\n    {\n        options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(applicationResolver);\n    }\n    if (JsonSerializer.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault)\n    {\n        options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(CreateReflectionResolver());\n    }\n\n    return options;\n}\n\n// src/Components/Endpoints/src/Rendering/EndpointHtmlRenderer.Streaming.cs\nvar markerTypeInfo = ServerComponentSerializationSettings.JsonSerializationOptions\n    .GetTypeInfo(typeof(ComponentMarker));\nvar serializedStartRecord = JsonSerializer.Serialize(marker, markerTypeInfo);\n\nvar endMarkerTypeInfo = ServerComponentSerializationSettings.JsonSerializationOptions\n    .GetTypeInfo(typeof(ComponentEndMarker));\nvar serializedEndRecord = JsonSerializer.Serialize(endMarker, endMarkerTypeInfo);\n```\n\nThe same options-owned contract rule applies to cached render fragments and marker serializers/deserializers. Raw marker tests assert lowercase `type`/`prerenderId`, absence of PascalCase names, and omission of null-only fields on both start and end comments.\n\n**Provider-scoped application composition.** Registration is additive, but resolution snapshots the list once when the provider creates the singleton resolver.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Web/src/Metadata/ComponentJsonMetadataResolver.cs\ninternal sealed class ComponentJsonMetadataResolver : IComponentJsonMetadataResolver\n{\n    public ComponentJsonMetadataResolver(IOptions<ComponentJsonMetadataOptions> options)\n    {\n        var resolvers = options.Value.Resolvers;\n        JsonTypeInfoResolver = resolvers.Count switch\n        {\n            0 => null,\n            1 => resolvers[0],\n            _ => System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfoResolver.Combine([.. resolvers]),\n        };\n    }\n\n    public IJsonTypeInfoResolver? JsonTypeInfoResolver { get; }\n}\n\n// src/Components/Components/src/PersistentState/PersistentStateSerializationOptions.cs\n// Every manager gets fresh options: framework first, its provider's app contracts next, reflection last.\npublic static JsonSerializerOptions Create(IJsonTypeInfoResolver? applicationResolver)\n{\n    var options = new JsonSerializerOptions(JsonSerializerOptionsProvider.Options);\n    options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Clear();\n    options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(PersistentStateJsonContext.Default);\n\n    if (applicationResolver is not null)\n    {\n        options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(applicationResolver);\n    }\n    if (JsonSerializer.IsReflectionEnabledByDefault)\n    {\n        options.TypeInfoResolverChain.Add(CreateReflectionResolver());\n    }\n\n    return options;\n}\n```\n\nConsumers fall into three identical ownership groups: persistence (`ComponentStatePersistenceManager`/`PersistentComponentState`), Server/Endpoints markers and Session (serializer/deserializer instances), and protected storage (DI-owned options). Directly constructed legacy instances retain shared compatibility options; DI-created instances snapshot the current provider.\n\n**JS payloads.** `JSRuntime` now installs reflection explicitly only when available and serializes outbound arguments through the existing `object[]` type-info contract. Web renderers place fixed contracts and converter-backed references ahead of application contracts.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Web/src/WebRenderer.cs\n// Fixed wire types are first; converter-owned object/stream references do not need reflected members;\n// app payloads follow; JSRuntime's compatibility reflection resolver remains last.\nvar resolvers = jsonOptions.TypeInfoResolverChain;\nPlaceResolverAt(resolvers, WebRendererSerializerContext.Default, 0);\nPlaceResolverAt(resolvers, WebJSInteropSerializerContext.Default, 1);\nPlaceResolverAt(resolvers, ConverterBackedTypeInfoResolver.Instance, 2);\nif (serviceProvider.GetService<IComponentJsonMetadataResolver>()?.JsonTypeInfoResolver is { } applicationResolver)\n{\n    PlaceResolverAt(resolvers, applicationResolver, 3);\n}\n\n// src/JSInterop/Microsoft.JSInterop/src/JSRuntime.cs\nvar argsJson = args is not null && args.Length != 0\n    ? JsonSerializer.Serialize(args, JsonSerializerOptions.GetTypeInfo(typeof(object[])))\n    : \"[]\";\n```\n\nThe equivalent inbound deltas are explicit type-info overloads for custom events and JS component parameters; `EventArgs.Empty` needs no contract. Navigation payloads send the Server renderer ID as its integer wire representation.\n\n**WebAssembly host timing and order.** Initial prerender parameter deserialization is deferred until after service-provider creation, so it can use that host's resolver snapshot. Root-update operations use the same host-owned context. Registered marker-backed roots are then inserted before manual mappings, retaining historical startup precedence and preserving order within both groups.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/WebAssembly/WebAssembly/src/Services/WebAssemblyHostSerializationContext.cs\npublic WebAssemblyHostSerializationContext(RootTypeCache rootComponentCache, IServiceProvider services)\n{\n    _rootComponentCache = rootComponentCache;\n    var resolver = ComponentJsonMetadata.GetApplicationResolver(services);\n    ComponentOptions = WebAssemblyComponentSerializationSettings.CreateOptions(resolver);\n    JSInteropOptions = DefaultWebAssemblyJSRuntime.Instance.CreateHostJsonSerializerOptions(resolver);\n    _parameterDeserializer = new WebAssemblyComponentParameterDeserializer(\n        new ComponentParametersTypeCache(),\n        ComponentOptions);\n}\n\n// src/Components/WebAssembly/WebAssembly/src/Hosting/WebAssemblyHostBuilder.cs\nvar registeredMappings = new RootComponentMapping[registeredComponents.Length];\nfor (var i = 0; i < registeredComponents.Length; i++)\n{\n    var registeredComponent = registeredComponents[i];\n    var componentType = _rootComponentCache!.GetRootType(\n        registeredComponent.Assembly!,\n        registeredComponent.TypeName!)\n        ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Registered root component type was not found.\");\n\n    var parameters = serializationContext.DeserializeComponentParameters(registeredComponent);\n    registeredMappings[i] = new RootComponentMapping(\n        componentType,\n        registeredComponent.PrerenderId!,\n        parameters.Parameters);\n}\n\nfor (var i = 0; i < registeredMappings.Length; i++)\n{\n    RootComponents.Insert(i, registeredMappings[i]);\n}\n```\n\n**Protected storage dispatch.** The generic path first looks for a closed typed serializer; otherwise it resolves generated JSON metadata from the provider-owned options. Protection and browser I/O are unchanged.\n\n```csharp\n// src/Components/Server/src/ProtectedBrowserStorage/ProtectedBrowserStorage.cs\nprivate string Protect<TValue>(string purpose, TValue value)\n{\n    var serializer = _services?.GetService<ProtectedBrowserStorageSerializer<TValue>>();\n    var data = serializer is null\n        ? JsonSerializer.Serialize(\n            value,\n            _serializerOptions.GetTypeInfo(value?.GetType() ?? typeof(TValue)))\n        : serializer.Serialize(value);\n    var protector = GetOrCreateCachedProtector(purpose);\n\n    return protector.Protect(data);\n}\n\nprivate TValue Unprotect<TValue>(string purpose, string protectedJson)\n{\n    var protector = GetOrCreateCachedProtector(purpose);\n    var data = protector.Unprotect(protectedJson);\n    var serializer = _services?.GetService<ProtectedBrowserStorageSerializer<TValue>>();\n\n    return serializer is null\n        ? (TValue)JsonSerializer.Deserialize(data, _serializerOptions.GetTypeInfo(typeof(TValue)))!\n        : serializer.Deserialize(data);\n}\n```\n\n## Outcome\n\n| Equivalence class | Validation/proof |\n|---|---|\n| Fixed framework contracts and reflection-last fallback | Reflection-disabled remote tests; persistent-state/TempData/initializer coverage; LinkabilityChecker build succeeded with 0 warnings/errors |\n| Marker and render-fragment protocol | Full Endpoints suite **813/0**; focused marker/cache tests **75/0**; raw start/end JSON assertions; representative Server interactive E2E passed |\n| Provider composition and isolation | Tests compose multiple contexts and prove an existing provider cannot observe later registrations; Web suite **316/0**, Server suite **405/0** |\n| Web/JS payloads | Explicit outbound/inbound type-info coverage, converter-backed reference coverage, and focused JSInterop serialization tests |\n| WebAssembly host ownership and ordering | WebAssembly suite **55/0**; two registered + two manual mapping order test; targeted `ClientRenderingMultpleComponentsTest.CanRenderMultipleRootComponents` passed in Debug JIT |\n| Protected storage | Typed serializer, runtime-type fallback, direct-construction compatibility, failure behavior, and API baseline coverage |\n| Cross-project integration | Dependency-aware Components E2ETest Debug and Release builds succeeded with 0 warnings/errors; shared nullable contexts compile when linked into nullable-disabled projects |\n\nRestack verification against current `main`: all **14/14** commits are patch-identical (`range-diff` `=` and matching stable patch IDs), with no dropped or repaired PR patches. Post-restack validation passed Components **36/0**, Web **9/0**, Endpoints **45/0**, Server **51/0**, WebAssembly **5/0**, JSInterop **56/0**, plus the dependency-aware Components E2ETest compile gate with 0 warnings/errors.\n\nThis PR remains independently reviewable against `main`; subsequent stack layers depend on its application JSON registration and host-isolated serializer composition.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68295/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70200","id":6137636082,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABL_jkAw","number":70200,"title":"Reduce allocations in QueryHelpers.AddQueryString","user":{"login":"davidfowl","id":95136,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1MTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95136?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfowl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"labels":[{"id":5058451585,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABLYHYgQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/pending-ci-rerun","name":"pending-ci-rerun","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"When assigned to a PR indicates that the CI checks should be rerun","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5572431303,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABTCSNxw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-networking","name":"area-networking","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes servers, yarp, json patch, bedrock, websockets, http client factory, and http abstractions","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-10-31T17:16:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T22:07:31Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70200","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70200","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70200.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70200.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"# Reduce allocations in QueryHelpers.AddQueryString\n\n- [x] You've read the [Contributor Guide](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) and [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/CODE-OF-CONDUCT.md).\n- [x] You've included unit or integration tests for your change, where applicable.\n- [x] You've included inline docs for your change, where applicable.\n- [ ] There's an open issue for the PR that you are making.\n\nFewer allocations and faster QueryHelpers.AddQueryString.\n\n## Description\n`QueryHelpers.AddQueryString` builds its result with a default-capacity `StringBuilder`, which grows chunk by chunk. The single name/value overload also wraps the pair in an array and goes through `IEnumerable` enumeration. The single-pair overload runs on hot paths such as cookie authentication login/access-denied redirects (`ReturnUrl`), and the dictionary overload runs when building OAuth/OIDC challenge URLs.\n\nChanges (all internal to `QueryHelpers`, no public API change):\n- **Both overloads** build into the shared `ValueStringBuilder`, starting on `stackalloc char[256]` and moving to `ArrayPool<char>` for longer output. Names and values are encoded in place with the span-based `UrlEncoder.Encode(ReadOnlySpan<char>, Span<char>, ...)`, so the result string is the only allocation. Growth is done locally, so pooled buffers are cleared before they're returned.\n- **`AddQueryString(string uri, string name, string value)`** no longer wraps the pair in an array and enumerates it. The separator is still decided exactly as before (is there a `?` before the first `#`).\n\nThe output is identical: same separators, same `UrlEncoder.Default` encoding, `null` values skipped, anchor preserved.\n\n### Benchmark\n`QueryHelpersAddQueryStringBenchmark` (added): BenchmarkDotNet InProcess (`--config perflab`, 3 warmup / 15 iterations), 3 interleaved rounds, mean of the rounds. \"Previous\" is the earlier `string.Create`/`Encode(string)` revision of this PR (cfd749c).\n\n| Case | main | previous | PR | main alloc | previous alloc | PR alloc |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ReturnUrl` (single pair, value needs encoding) | 153.3 ns | 86.1 ns | 84.2 ns (−45%) | 600 B | 216 B | 136 B (−77%) |\n| `Simple` (single pair, no encoding) | 65.0 ns | 26.4 ns | 45.6 ns (−30%) | 304 B | 56 B | 56 B (−82%) |\n| `LongValue` (602-char value, no encoding) | 242.2 ns | 105.5 ns | 200.3 ns (−17%) | 2,768 B | 1,264 B | 1,264 B (−54%) |\n| `EncodeHeavy` (short non-ASCII/reserved value) | 202.6 ns | 154.1 ns | 149.3 ns (−26%) | 760 B | 392 B | 208 B (−73%) |\n| `OAuth` (7-entry dictionary) | 484.1 ns | 363.8 ns | 420.2 ns (−13%) | 2,072 B | 952 B | 768 B (−63%) |\n\nPercentages are relative to main. Compared with the previous revision, the span-based encoder saves allocations whenever something gets encoded, but it's slower when nothing does, because `Encode(string)` returns the input instance without copying.\n\n### Tests\nAdded `AddQueryStringMatchesReferenceImplementation`, which compares both the single-pair and the enumerable overloads against the previous `StringBuilder` algorithm. Cases cover empty URIs, a trailing `?`, `#` inside the anchor and multiple `#`, a `?` inside the fragment, non-ASCII and surrogate pairs, characters that need encoding, `null` values, 1,400-char keys and values (longer once encoded) that force the pooled buffer to grow, lone surrogates, a 300-char value that expands 9× when encoded (several regrowths), surrogate pairs straddling the 256-char stack buffer, and a URI longer than the stack buffer. A mutation that skips regrowth after `DestinationTooSmall` fails all 12 cases. All 518 WebUtilities tests pass.\n\n**🤖 Posted by ASP.NET Core Perf 2 (AI Agent)**\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70200/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1143301,"client_id":"Iv23ctzlsVrAf9UtZ48B","slug":"copilot-swe-agent","node_id":"A_kwHNJr_OABFyBQ","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Copilot SWE Agent","description":"","external_url":"https://github.com/features/copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","created_at":"2025-02-12T20:26:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T17:13:09Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","actions_variables":"read","administration":"read","agent_secrets":"read","agent_tasks":"write","agent_variables":"read","checks":"read","code_quality":"read","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","discussions":"write","environments":"write","gists":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","organization_agent_secrets":"read","organization_agent_variables":"read","organization_noodles":"write","packages":"read","plugin_gateway_connections":"write","pull_requests":"write","secrets":"read","secret_scanning_alerts":"read","security_events":"read","statuses":"read","vulnerability_alerts":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":[]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/69769","id":5812860745,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABH8-yuA","number":69769,"title":"Reduce Blazor Server Native AOT publish warnings","user":{"login":"PreethikaSelvam","id":125338432,"node_id":"U_kgDOB3iDQA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125338432?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam","html_url":"https://github.com/PreethikaSelvam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PreethikaSelvam/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2209519932,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjA5NTE5OTMy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/community-contribution","name":"community-contribution","color":"c2e0c6","default":false,"description":"Indicates that the PR has been added by a community member","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5058451585,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABLYHYgQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/pending-ci-rerun","name":"pending-ci-rerun","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"When assigned to a PR indicates that the CI checks should be rerun","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-10-12T11:22:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T14:22:41Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T14:22:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/69769","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/69769","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/69769.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/69769.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Description\r\n\r\nThis PR partially addresses #69270 by fixing Blazor Server trimming and Native AOT warnings that have safe, framework-owned solutions.\r\n\r\nThe changes:\r\n\r\n- Correct the Endpoints linker substitution resource to target `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Endpoints`.\r\n- Use source-generated JSON metadata for closed framework payloads, including import maps, resource collections, TempData and session envelopes, JavaScript initializers, persisted circuit markers, WebAssembly parameter definitions, and streaming component markers.\r\n- Preserve application-configured HTTP JSON converters, encoders, naming policies, and resolvers for the JavaScript initializers endpoint.\r\n- Add reflection-disabled regression coverage for generated initializer metadata and configured HTTP JSON converter precedence.\r\n- Keep trimming diagnostics visible where supported instance-root, custom-activator, arbitrary-object, session, or TempData paths lack enforceable preservation contracts.\r\n- Keep unresolved component discovery, arbitrary-object parameter assignment, root-component, and JS interop warnings visible.\r\n- Remove `IL2101` from `WarningsNotAsErrors` and add it to `WarningsAsErrors` so regressions fail the Native AOT build even though other ILC warnings remain nonfatal.\r\n\r\n### Warning results\r\n\r\n| Warning | Baseline | Fixed | Remaining | Reason remaining |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\r\n| `IL2101` | 2 emitted from 1 defect | 2 | 0 | Fixed by correcting the linker substitution assembly. |\r\n| `IL2062` | 1 | 0 | 1 | Component discovery needs generated metadata or an enforced preservation contract. |\r\n| `IL2065` | 1 | 0 | 1 | Assembly-scanned `[JSInvokable]` methods need explicit or generated preservation. |\r\n| `IL2067` | 1 | 0 | 1 | Root-component type requirements are not enforced at the incoming boundary. |\r\n| `IL2072` | 7 | 0 | 7 | Supported instance-root, custom-activator, arbitrary-object, root-component, and session serialization paths do not have enforceable preserved-type flow. |\r\n| `IL2080` | 2 | 0 | 2 | Session and TempData getter reflection receives runtime component types without enforceable property-preservation annotations. |\r\n| `IL3050` | 51 emitted warnings | 11 | 40 | Remaining paths use application-defined types or inherently dynamic operations. |\r\n| `IL2026` | 20 direct and 2 application call-site diagnostics | Not quantified | Not quantified | This warning family remains suppressed by the test harness. |\r\n| `IL2057` | 1 | 0 | 1 | Runtime type resolution requires generated metadata or an application type registry. |\r\n| Razor-generated `IL2110` | 5 propagated | 0 | 5 | Requires a Razor compiler or source-generator change. |\r\n| Razor-generated `IL2111` | 8 propagated | 0 | 8 | Requires a Razor compiler or source-generator change. |\r\n\r\nThe remaining warnings require generated application metadata, explicit preservation contracts, an application type registry, broader Native AOT design work, or Razor compiler changes. They are intentionally not hidden with blanket suppressions.\r\n\r\n### Validation\r\n\r\nComponents Endpoints tests: **881 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1072\" height=\"541\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01c4c4a6-5da9-49cf-ac84-2bdab6d6dcdb\" />\r\nComponents Server tests: **395 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1151\" height=\"653\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/772a8955-15a2-4539-a66a-bead29dae712\" />\r\nJSInterop tests: **170 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1083\" height=\"653\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc19ffb4-f495-4915-bbf2-67d9689dd987\" />\r\nFocused `ParameterViewTest` coverage: **64 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1847\" height=\"550\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2e926969-6f95-4998-9aa3-971b72d65917\" />\r\n`ComponentFactoryTest` and `CascadingParameterStateTest`: **44 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1238\" height=\"702\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ee2632f9-2b8f-48cb-bb0f-b87222f4c781\" />\r\nSession and TempData cascading-value tests: **22 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1851\" height=\"698\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c5ac810b-0469-4f4c-8df4-21299b0a7e55\" />\r\nReflection-disabled JavaScript initializer tests: **2 passed, 0 failed**\r\n<img width=\"1642\" height=\"801\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/486ea61d-9d3d-447b-a7be-6be63df79016\" />\r\n\r\nNative AOT analysis:\r\n\r\n- `IL2072`: **7**\r\n  - Two `ComponentProperties.SetProperties` arbitrary-object diagnostics\r\n  - One session serialization metadata diagnostic\r\n  - One instance-based cascading-parameter diagnostic\r\n  - One custom-activator property-injection diagnostic\r\n  - Two root-component type-flow diagnostics\r\n- `IL2080`: **2**\r\n  - One session property-getter diagnostic\r\n  - One TempData property-getter diagnostic\r\n- `IL2101`: **0**\r\n- `IL3050`: **40**\r\n- Unresolved `IL2062`, `IL2065`, `IL2067`, `IL2072`, and `IL2080` diagnostics remain visible as intended.\r\n\r\nNative AOT analysis completed.\r\n\r\nFixes [#69270](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69270)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/69769/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64749","id":3723661013,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde864lIi9","number":64749,"title":"TempData support for Blazor","user":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/378","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/378","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/378/labels","id":14553365,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84A3hEV","number":378,"title":"11.0-preview2","description":"","creator":{"login":"danroth27","id":1874516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzQ1MTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1874516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27","html_url":"https://github.com/danroth27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":84,"state":"closed","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:25:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T17:44:36Z","due_on":"2026-03-10T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2026-04-21T08:57:01Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-12T14:40:23Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:43:51Z","closed_at":"2026-02-03T11:53:51Z","assignee":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/64749","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64749","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64749.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64749.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-03T11:53:51Z"},"body":"# TempData support for Blazor\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR adds native TempData support for Blazor Server-Side Rendering (SSR), similar to the existing [TempData in MVC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/app-state#tempdata). TempData provides a mechanism for storing data that persists between HTTP requests, making it ideal for scenarios like:\r\n\r\n- Flash messages after form submissions\r\n- Passing data during redirects (POST-Redirect-GET pattern)\r\n- One-time notifications\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n### Core Components\r\n\r\n| Component | Description |\r\n|-----------|-------------|\r\n| `ITempData` | Interface defining the TempData contract, extends `IDictionary<string, object?>` |\r\n| `TempData` | Concrete implementation with lazy loading and automatic cleanup |\r\n| `ITempDataProvider` | Abstraction for storage backends |\r\n| `CookieTempDataProvider` | Default provider using encrypted cookies |\r\n| `SessionStorageTempDataProvider` | Alternative provider using session storage |\r\n| `JsonTempDataSerializer` | JSON-based serialization for TempData values |\r\n\r\n### Integration\r\n\r\nTempData is automatically registered when calling `AddRazorComponents()` and is provided as a cascading value. The default cookie-based provider is used unless explicitly configured otherwise.\r\n\r\n### Public API\r\n\r\n\r\n### ITempData Interface\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nnamespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components;\r\n\r\n/// <summary>\r\n/// Provides a dictionary for storing data that is needed for subsequent requests.\r\n/// Data stored in TempData is automatically removed after it is read unless\r\n/// Keep() or Keep(string) is called, or it is accessed via Peek(string).\r\n/// </summary>\r\npublic interface ITempData : IDictionary<string, object?>\r\n{\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Gets the value associated with the specified key and then schedules it for deletion.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    object? Get(string key);\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Returns the value associated with the specified key without marking it for deletion.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    object? Peek(string key);\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Marks all keys in the dictionary for retention. Values will be available on the next request.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    void Keep();\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Marks the specified key for retention. The value will be available on the next request.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    void Keep(string key);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### ITempDataProvider Interface\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nnamespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Endpoints;\r\n\r\n/// <summary>\r\n/// Provides an abstraction for a provider that stores and retrieves temporary data.\r\n/// </summary>\r\npublic interface ITempDataProvider\r\n{\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Loads temporary data from the given <see cref=\"HttpContext\"/>.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    IDictionary<string, object?> LoadTempData(HttpContext context);\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Saves temporary data to the given <see cref=\"HttpContext\"/>.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    void SaveTempData(HttpContext context, IDictionary<string, object?> values);\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Service Collection Extensions\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nnamespace Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;\r\n\r\npublic static class TempDataProviderServiceCollectionExtensions\r\n{\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Registers the cookie-based TempData provider (default).\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public static IServiceCollection AddCookieTempDataValueProvider(\r\n        this IServiceCollection services,\r\n        Action<CookieTempDataProviderOptions>? configure = null);\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// Registers the session-based TempData provider.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public static IServiceCollection AddSessionStorageTempDataValueProvider(\r\n        this IServiceCollection services);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### CookieTempDataProviderOptions\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nnamespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Endpoints;\r\n\r\npublic class CookieTempDataProviderOptions\r\n{\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// The name of the cookie. Default: \".AspNetCore.Components.TempData\"\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public string CookieName { get; set; }\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// The cookie path. Default: \"/\"\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public string? Path { get; set; }\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// The cookie domain.\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public string? Domain { get; set; }\r\n\r\n    /// <summary>\r\n    /// The SameSite attribute of the cookie. Default: SameSiteMode.Strict\r\n    /// </summary>\r\n    public SameSiteMode SameSite { get; set; }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\n**TempData behavior** (`src/Components/Endpoints/test/TempData/TempDataTest.cs`):\r\n- Indexer get/set operations\r\n- `Get` returns value and removes from retained keys\r\n- `Peek` returns value without removing from retained keys\r\n- `Keep()` retains all keys\r\n- `Keep(string)` retains specific key\r\n- `ContainsKey` returns correct results\r\n- `Remove` removes key and returns success\r\n- `Save` returns only retained keys\r\n- `Load` populates data from dictionary\r\n- `Clear` removes all data\r\n- `WasLoaded` tracks lazy loading state\r\n- Keys are case-insensitive\r\n\r\n**JSON Serialization** (`src/Components/Endpoints/test/TempData/JsonTempDataSerializerTest.cs`):\r\n- Serialize/deserialize primitive types (string, int, bool, Guid, DateTimeOffset)\r\n- Serialize/deserialize arrays (string[], int[])\r\n- Serialize/deserialize dictionaries\r\n- Handle empty arrays and null values\r\n- Throw for unsupported types\r\n\r\n**Cookie Provider** (`src/Components/Endpoints/test/TempData/CookieTempDataProviderTest.cs`):\r\n- Load returns empty dictionary when no cookie exists\r\n- Save deletes cookie when no data\r\n- Save sets encrypted cookie when data exists\r\n- Round-trip preserves all supported types\r\n- Handle invalid/corrupted cookies gracefully\r\n\r\n**Service Registration** (`src/Components/Endpoints/test/TempData/TempDataProviderServiceExtensionsTest.cs`):\r\n- Cookie provider registers expected services\r\n- Session provider registers expected services\r\n- Custom options are applied correctly\r\n\r\n### E2E Tests\r\n\r\n**Integration tests** (`src/Components/test/E2ETest/Tests/TempDataTest.cs`):\r\n- Values persist after same-page redirect\r\n- Values persist across different pages\r\n- `Peek` preserves values for subsequent requests\r\n- `Keep()` retains all values\r\n- `Keep(key)` retains specific value\r\n- `Remove()` deletes values\r\n- Works with both cookie and session providers\r\n\r\n\r\n## API usage\r\n\r\n**Basic form with flash messages:**\r\n```razor\r\n@page \"/my-form\"\r\n@inject NavigationManager NavigationManager\r\n\r\n<p id=\"message\">@_message</p>\r\n\r\n<form method=\"post\" @formname=\"MyForm\" @onsubmit=\"HandleSubmit\">\r\n    <AntiforgeryToken />\r\n    <input type=\"text\" name=\"Name\" />\r\n    <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\r\n</form>\r\n\r\n@code {\r\n    [CascadingParameter]\r\n    public ITempData? TempData { get; set; }\r\n\r\n    private string? _message;\r\n\r\n    protected override void OnInitialized()\r\n    {\r\n        // Get removes the value after reading (one-time use)\r\n        _message = TempData?.Get(\"Message\") as string ?? \"No message\";\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    private void HandleSubmit()\r\n    {\r\n        // Set success message\r\n        TempData![\"Message\"] = \"Form submitted successfully!\";\r\n        \r\n        // Redirect - message will be available on next request\r\n        NavigationManager.NavigateTo(\"/my-form\", forceLoad: true);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Reading without consuming (Peek):**\r\n```razor\r\n@code {\r\n    protected override void OnInitialized()\r\n    {\r\n        // Peek reads without removing - value available on next request too\r\n        var notification = TempData?.Peek(\"Notification\") as string;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Keeping values for another request:**\r\n```razor\r\n@code {\r\n    protected override void OnInitialized()\r\n    {\r\n        var message = TempData?.Get(\"Message\") as string;\r\n        \r\n        // Keep this specific value for one more request\r\n        TempData?.Keep(\"Message\");\r\n        \r\n        // Or keep all values\r\n        TempData?.Keep();\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Design Decisions\r\n\r\n1. **Cascading Parameter**: TempData is provided as a cascading value rather than requiring explicit injection, making it easily accessible throughout the component tree.\r\n\r\n2. **Lazy Loading**: TempData is only loaded from storage when first accessed, avoiding unnecessary cookie parsing for requests that don't use TempData.\r\n\r\n3. **Cookie as Default**: Cookies are the default storage mechanism (matching MVC behavior) because they don't require additional middleware configuration.\r\n\r\n4. **Data Protection**: Cookie values are encrypted using ASP.NET Core Data Protection to prevent tampering and information disclosure.\r\n\r\n5. **Response.OnStarting**: TempData is saved using `Response.OnStarting` callback to ensure it's persisted even if the component doesn't explicitly save it.\r\n\r\nFixes #49683","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64749/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65722","id":4051028163,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde87JWU3J","number":65722,"title":"Fix TempData lazy loading bugs","user":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/379","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/379","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/379/labels","id":14553368,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84A3hEY","number":379,"title":"11.0-preview3","description":"","creator":{"login":"danroth27","id":1874516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzQ1MTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1874516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27","html_url":"https://github.com/danroth27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":200,"state":"closed","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:26:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T09:31:23Z","due_on":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2026-05-25T09:31:23Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-10T11:06:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T09:44:45Z","closed_at":"2026-03-10T16:03:40Z","assignee":{"login":"dariatiurina","id":110841893,"node_id":"U_kgDOBptQJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110841893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina","html_url":"https://github.com/dariatiurina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dariatiurina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/65722","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65722","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65722.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65722.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-10T16:03:40Z"},"body":"## Fix TempData lazy loading bugs\r\n\r\nSeveral `TempData` methods accessed the `_data` backing field directly instead of the `Data` property, bypassing lazy loading. Additionally, `Get` and `Remove` had an ordering issue \r\nwhere modifying `_retainedKeys` before reading the value could trigger lazy load and lose the result.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n- **`Get` / `Remove`**: Read the value *before* modifying `_retainedKeys` to preserve correct return values when the call triggers lazy loading\r\n- **`Keep` / `TempDataEnumerator`**: Use `Data` property instead of `_data` field to ensure lazy loading is triggered\r\n- Added 5 unit tests covering lazy-load scenarios for `Get`, indexer, `Remove`, `Keep`, and enumeration\r\n- Fixed test asset `TempDataComponent.razor` to read values before checking `ContainsKey`\r\n\r\nFixes #65720\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65722/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70436","id":6312232505,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABOK01fQ","number":70436,"title":"[release/11.0] Mark 11.0.0 APIs as shipped","user":{"login":"wtgodbe","id":14283640,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjgzNjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14283640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe","html_url":"https://github.com/wtgodbe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1465509900,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDY1NTA5OTAw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/tell-mode","name":"tell-mode","color":"e989f9","default":false,"description":"Indicates a PR which is being merged during tell-mode","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:30:48Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T19:15:44Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T19:15:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70436","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70436","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70436.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70436.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T19:15:42Z"},"body":"## Description\n\nMark APIs released in ASP.NET Core 11.0.0 as shipped, following dotnet/aspnetcore#64316 and dotnet/aspnetcore#58060.\n\nCompanion main PR: dotnet/aspnetcore#70437.\n\nRan `eng/scripts/mark-shipped.ps1` with the API set from the `v11.0.0` tag (`1def4cdc07dc10fc267136060e3ef5c1a96d4a99`): move 496 additions into shipped baselines and apply 101 `*REMOVED*` entries. The change is limited to 82 API baseline files.\n\nThe only API left in any release/11.0 `PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt` is `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.QuickGrid.Paginator.AdditionalAttributes` (getter and setter). It was added after the 11.0.0 tag by servicing-approved dotnet/aspnetcore#70093, so it remains unshipped for the next servicing release.\n\n## Customer Impact\n\nRelease bookkeeping only. No source, runtime behavior, or effective API-surface changes.\n\n## Regression?\n\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\n## Risk\n\n- [ ] High\n- [ ] Medium\n- [x] Low\n\nUses the existing shipping script and the tagged 11.0.0 API surface rather than treating post-GA servicing additions as already shipped.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] Manual: reviewed the API movements and the remaining QuickGrid servicing API.\n- [x] Automated: audited all 171 shipped/unshipped API pairs, checked exact GA membership and unchanged effective API surfaces, and ran `git diff --check`.\n- [x] Cross-branch: all 171 mapped shipped baselines match the companion main change byte-for-byte.\n\nFull repository builds were not run locally; CI validation is pending.\n\n## Packaging changes reviewed?\n\n- [ ] Yes\n- [ ] No\n- [x] N/A\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70436/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70437","id":6312234894,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABOK09dg","number":70437,"title":"Mark 11.0.0 APIs as shipped on main","user":{"login":"wtgodbe","id":14283640,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjgzNjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14283640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe","html_url":"https://github.com/wtgodbe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtgodbe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":792032421,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTIwMzI0MjE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-dataprotection","name":"area-dataprotection","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: DataProtection","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1118585221,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTE4NTg1MjIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-mvc","name":"area-mvc","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: MVC, Actions and Controllers, Localization, CORS, most templates","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1118663032,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTE4NjYzMDMy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-auth","name":"area-auth","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: authentication, authorization, OAuth, OIDC, and access token validation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1140884961,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTQwODg0OTYx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-signalr","name":"area-signalr","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: SignalR clients and servers","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1143445347,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTQzNDQ1MzQ3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-identity","name":"area-identity","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Identity and providers","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5351896046,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABPv9z7g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-minimal","name":"area-minimal","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes minimal APIs, endpoint filters, parameter binding, request delegate generator etc","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5572431303,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABTCSNxw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-networking","name":"area-networking","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes servers, yarp, json patch, bedrock, websockets, http client factory, and http abstractions","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5572432874,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABTCST6g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-middleware","name":"area-middleware","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: URL rewrite, redirect, response cache/compression, session, and other general middlewares","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":5644268170,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAQzde88AAAABUGyyig","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-routing","name":"area-routing","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: endpoint routing and URL matching","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/408","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408/labels","id":17341069,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84BCJqN","number":408,"title":"12.0-preview1","description":null,"creator":{"login":"dotnet-milestone-bot[bot]","id":286398033,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOERIWUQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9141961?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dotnet-milestone-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":6,"closed_issues":579,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-08-17T16:20:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T22:43:39Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:30:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T14:54:19Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T19:15:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70437","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70437","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70437.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70437.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T19:15:35Z"},"body":"## Description\n\nPort the 11.0.0 shipped-API bookkeeping to main, following dotnet/aspnetcore#64319 and dotnet/aspnetcore#58897.\n\nCompanion release/11.0 PR: dotnet/aspnetcore#70436.\n\nRan `eng/scripts/mark-shipped.ps1` with only the exact API set from the `v11.0.0` tag (`1def4cdc07dc10fc267136060e3ef5c1a96d4a99`) eligible to move: 496 additions and 101 `*REMOVED*` entries across 82 baseline files. Newer APIs were excluded from the shipping pass and preserved in their unshipped files.\n\nHandled the six `PublicAPI/net11.0` to `PublicAPI/net12.0` directory renames and the JSInterop directory relocation. All 171 mapped shipped baseline files are byte-identical to the companion release/11.0 change.\n\n## APIs intentionally left unshipped\n\nAll **615 new 12.0 baseline entries** remain in the following byte-for-byte unchanged files:\n\n| Area | Entries | API families / full inventory |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Components.AI | 359 | [UI agents and state, conversation/chat components, content and tool blocks, rich-text/Markdown nodes](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/wtgodbe/mark-11-api-shipped-main/src/Components/AI/src/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt) |\n| Components.Platform | 187 | [Browser platform services, Window/Navigator/Screen, cookies, storage/events, URL APIs and DI extensions](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/wtgodbe/mark-11-api-shipped-main/src/Components/Platform/src/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt) |\n| Identity.Core | 69 | [Passkey endpoint configuration and mapping, request/response types, conditional-creation and credential-signal APIs](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/wtgodbe/mark-11-api-shipped-main/src/Identity/Core/src/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt) |\n\nQuickGrid's `Paginator.AdditionalAttributes` getter and setter also remain unshipped on both branches. These are post-11.0.0, servicing-approved additions from dotnet/aspnetcore#70093, not APIs shipped in 11.0.0.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Audited all 173 shipped/unshipped API pairs on main.\n- Confirmed every shipped addition/removal belongs to the tagged 11.0.0 set.\n- Confirmed the effective API surface is unchanged for every pair.\n- Confirmed all 615 new 12.0 entries remain in byte-unchanged unshipped files.\n- Confirmed all 171 mapped shipped baselines match release/11.0 byte-for-byte.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n\nFull repository builds were not run locally; CI validation is pending.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70437/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70187","id":6136745759,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde88AAAABL-3V8w","number":70187,"title":"Reduce allocations in DataProtection string Protect/Unprotect","user":{"login":"davidfowl","id":95136,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1MTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95136?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfowl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfowl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"labels":[{"id":792032421,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTIwMzI0MjE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-dataprotection","name":"area-dataprotection","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: DataProtection","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/408","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/408/labels","id":17341069,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84BCJqN","number":408,"title":"12.0-preview1","description":null,"creator":{"login":"dotnet-milestone-bot[bot]","id":286398033,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOERIWUQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9141961?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dotnet-milestone-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dotnet-milestone-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":6,"closed_issues":579,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-08-17T16:20:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T22:43:39Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-31T15:47:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T04:11:50Z","closed_at":"2026-11-06T11:26:06Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/70187","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70187","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70187.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70187.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-06T11:26:06Z"},"body":"Reduce allocations in DataProtection string Protect/Unprotect\n\n## Description\n\n`DataProtectionCommonExtensions.Protect(string)` / `Unprotect(string)` (used by TempData, antiforgery-style consumers, and many apps) allocated a UTF-8 `byte[]` of the plaintext, then the protected `byte[]`, then the Base64Url string (and the reverse for `Unprotect`). On .NET, when the protector implements `ISpanDataProtector` (which `CreateProtector` always returns on .NET), these overloads now:\n\n- encode the string to UTF-8 into an `ArrayPool<byte>` buffer (cleared on return),\n- protect/unprotect into the shared `RefPooledArrayBufferWriter<byte>` seeded with a 256-byte stack buffer (rented arrays are cleared when outgrown and on dispose; the stack buffer is cleared after Unprotect),\n- Base64Url-encode directly from the written span (`WebEncoders.Base64UrlEncode(ReadOnlySpan<byte>)`).\n\n`Unprotect(string)` still uses `WebEncoders.Base64UrlDecode` so the accepted input format (base64 and base64url) is unchanged. Non-span protectors and non-.NET TFMs keep the existing code path.\n\nFound by profiling (EventPipe CPU + allocation sampling) realistic DataProtection scenarios: 59% of `str_protect` allocations were in `DataProtectionCommonExtensions` itself.\n\n### Benchmarks\nLinux x64, 2 cores, BenchmarkDotNet in-process, 3 interleaved rounds vs main (median). Cookie-style purpose chain, cached protector, default managed CBC+HMAC and AES-256-GCM.\n\n| Alg | Scenario | main | PR | main alloc | PR alloc |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CBC | Protect(string) 100 B | 10.03 us | 10.00 us | 2,040 B | 1,304 B (-36%) |\n| CBC | Protect(string) 2 KB | 14.99 us | 14.43 us | 12,281 B | 6,120 B (-50%) |\n| CBC | Unprotect(string) 100 B | 7.58 us | 7.68 us | 1,144 B | 1,016 B (-11%) |\n| CBC | Unprotect(string) 2 KB | 10.66 us | 10.57 us | 8,368 B | 6,432 B (-23%) |\n| GCM | Protect(string) 100 B | 8.03 us | 7.97 us | 1,152 B | 832 B (-28%) |\n| GCM | Protect(string) 2 KB | 9.57 us | 9.36 us | 9,584 B | 5,648 B (-41%) |\n| GCM | Unprotect(string) 100 B | 5.83 us | 5.79 us | 832 B | 704 B (-15%) |\n| GCM | Unprotect(string) 2 KB | 7.38 us | 7.08 us | 8,056 B | 6,120 B (-24%) |\n\nTime is neutral (within noise); the win is allocation.\n\n### Custom (byte[]-only) encryptors\nAll built-in encryptors (managed CBC/GCM, CNG CBC/GCM) implement `ISpanAuthenticatedEncryptor` and take the zero-copy path. For a custom `IAuthenticatedEncryptor` that only implements the byte[] API, `KeyRingBasedSpanDataProtector` falls back to copying the ciphertext span to an array, so `Unprotect(string)` pays one extra ciphertext-sized copy; `Protect(string)` is neutral. 728fd91610 removes the avoidable AAD copy in that fallback (`GetAadForKey` already returns an array). The same change and measurements are on #70191.\n\n### Security reasoning\n- **Payload format unchanged / byte-identical:** the span path calls the same key ring protector with the same plaintext bytes and AAD. New known-answer theory `StringProtect_SpanProtector_ProducesSamePayloadAsByteArrayPath` (CBC and GCM, 0 B–70 KB) uses a deterministic RNG to assert the string output equals `Base64UrlEncode(Protect(byte[]))` from the existing path, and round-trips both ways.\n- **Plaintext hygiene improves:** the UTF-8 plaintext buffer (protect) and the decrypted plaintext buffer (unprotect) are pooled and returned with `clearArray: true`; the shared writer now also clears every array it outgrows. Previously these plaintext `byte[]`s were left to the GC without being zeroed. No key material passes through these buffers.\n- **Nothing pooled is caller-reachable:** the writer is an internal `ref struct` scoped to a single call; only the resulting string (the same value as before) escapes.\n- **Exceptions unchanged:** invalid UTF-8 still throws from `SecureUtf8Encoding` (same type/message); invalid base64 still throws from `Base64UrlDecode`; protector exceptions propagate unchanged (covered by new tests). No public API change, no PublicAPI.*.txt changes, no unsafe code.\n- No crypto primitives, comparisons or validation logic are touched.\n\n### Overlap\nNo overlap with #70146 (managed encryptor internals); this change is in the Abstractions extension methods only and composes with it.\n\n### Tests\n- `Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Abstractions.Tests`: 36 passed (9 new span-path tests: growth, empty, invalid UTF-8, invalid base64, exception propagation).\n- `Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Tests`: 345 passed (new known-answer theory).\n\n🤖 Posted by ASP.NET Core Perf 2 (AI Agent)\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/70187/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1143301,"client_id":"Iv23ctzlsVrAf9UtZ48B","slug":"copilot-swe-agent","node_id":"A_kwHNJr_OABFyBQ","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/git